WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.151 --> 00:00:06.254
♪ ♪

00:00:06.255 --> 00:00:09.023
&gt;&gt; Greg: ON "SNL," PETE

00:00:09.024 --> 00:00:09.824
DAVIDSON APOLOGIZED TO

00:00:09.825 --> 00:00:11.826
CONGRESSMAN ELECT DAN CRENSHAW

00:00:11.827 --> 00:00:12.861
FOR MOCKING HIS WAR WOUND.

00:00:12.862 --> 00:00:16.364
&gt;&gt; I MADE A JOKE ABOUT

00:00:16.365 --> 00:00:19.033
LIEUTENANT COMMANDER DAN

00:00:19.034 --> 00:00:19.400
CRENSHAW.

00:00:19.401 --> 00:00:21.269
ON BEHALF OF THE SHOW AND

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.437
MYSELF, I APOLOGIZE.

00:00:22.438 --> 00:00:24.672
IT WAS A POOR CHOICE OF WORDS.

00:00:24.673 --> 00:00:26.508
THE MAN IS A WAR HERO AND HE

00:00:26.509 --> 00:00:28.243
DESERVES ALL THE RESPECT IN THE

00:00:28.244 --> 00:00:28.543
WORLD.

00:00:28.544 --> 00:00:31.446
&gt;&gt; Greg: THIS IS WHAT DAVIDSON

00:00:31.447 --> 00:00:32.046
HAD SAID INITIALLY ABOUT

00:00:32.047 --> 00:00:32.480
CRENSHAW.

00:00:32.481 --> 00:00:34.582
&gt;&gt; YOU MAY BE SURPRISED TO HEAR

00:00:34.583 --> 00:00:35.917
HE'S A CONGRESSIONAL CANDIDATE

00:00:35.918 --> 00:00:39.754
FROM TEXAS AND NOT A HIT MAN AND

00:00:39.755 --> 00:00:43.825
A PORNO MOVIE.

00:00:43.826 --> 00:00:47.629
I KNOW HE LOST HIS EYE IN WAR OR

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:48.630
WHATEVER.

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:50.031
&gt;&gt; Greg: REMEMBER CRENSHAW

00:00:50.032 --> 00:00:51.065
HADN'T DEMANDED AN APOLOGY.

00:00:51.066 --> 00:00:53.835
HE TAPPED THE BRAKES ON THE

00:00:53.836 --> 00:00:55.036
ALWAYS REVVING OUTRAGE MACHINE.

00:00:55.037 --> 00:00:57.639
&gt;&gt; I WANT TO GET AWAY FROM THIS

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:58.873
CULTURE WILL BE DEMAND APOLOGY

00:00:58.874 --> 00:01:00.108
EVERY TIME SOMEONE MISSED

00:01:00.109 --> 00:01:00.475
SPEAKS.

00:01:00.476 --> 00:01:02.510
THAT WOULD BE HEALTHY FOR OUR

00:01:02.511 --> 00:01:04.479
NATION TO GO IN THAT DIRECTION.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.614
WE DON'T NEED TO BE OUTWARDLY

00:01:06.615 --> 00:01:06.981
OUTRAGED.

00:01:06.982 --> 00:01:09.284
I DON'T NEED TO DEMAND

00:01:09.285 --> 00:01:09.651
APOLOGIES.

00:01:09.652 --> 00:01:10.685
&gt;&gt; Greg: BUT "SNL" KNEW WHAT

00:01:10.686 --> 00:01:13.888
IT HAD TO DO TO QUELL A P.R.

00:01:13.889 --> 00:01:14.322
NIGHTMARE.

00:01:14.323 --> 00:01:14.656
MAN UP.

00:01:14.657 --> 00:01:17.258
&gt;&gt; I'M SORRY.

00:01:17.259 --> 00:01:18.259
&gt;&gt; THANK YOU.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.295
I APPRECIATE YOU SAYING THAT.

00:01:20.296 --> 00:01:21.229
&gt;&gt; ARE WE GOOD?

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:22.130
&gt;&gt; WE ARE GOOD.

00:01:22.131 --> 00:01:31.206
APOLOGY ACCEPTED.

00:01:31.207 --> 00:01:31.573
♪ ♪

00:01:31.574 --> 00:01:33.841
&gt;&gt; ARIANA GRANDE.

00:01:33.842 --> 00:01:36.778
&gt;&gt; THIS IS PETE DAVIDSON.

00:01:36.779 --> 00:01:41.482
HE LOOKS LIKE IF THE METH FROM

00:01:41.483 --> 00:01:43.885
BREAKING BAD WAS A PERSON.

00:01:43.886 --> 00:01:45.887
&gt;&gt; Greg: FACE-TO-FACE, SO RARE

00:01:45.888 --> 00:01:47.889
THESE DAYS WHEN WE HIDE BEHIND

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:48.489
FIREWALLS AND LAWYERS.

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:51.059
"SNL" GAVE CRENSHAW THIS SPACE

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.628
TO SPEAK AT LENGTH ABOUT

00:01:53.629 --> 00:01:54.229
VETERANS AND UNITY.

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:55.830
&gt;&gt; AMERICANS CAN FORGIVE ONE

00:01:55.831 --> 00:01:56.831
ANOTHER.

00:01:56.832 --> 00:01:58.299
WE CAN REMEMBER WHAT BRINGS US

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.267
TOGETHER AS A COUNTRY AND STILL

00:01:59.268 --> 00:02:02.136
SEE THE GOOD IN EACH OTHER.

00:02:02.137 --> 00:02:03.004
THIS IS VETERANS DAY WEEKEND.

00:02:03.005 --> 00:02:05.073
WHICH MEANS IT'S A GOOD TIME FOR

00:02:05.074 --> 00:02:07.242
EVERY AMERICAN TO CONNECT WITH A

00:02:07.243 --> 00:02:07.842
VETERAN.

00:02:07.843 --> 00:02:10.311
TELL A VETERAN "NEVER FORGET."

00:02:10.312 --> 00:02:12.280
WHEN YOU SAY NEVER FORGET TO A

00:02:12.281 --> 00:02:13.548
VETERAN, YOU ARE IMPLYING THAT

00:02:13.549 --> 00:02:15.583
AS AN AMERICAN, YOU ARE IN IT

00:02:15.584 --> 00:02:16.317
WITH THEM.

00:02:16.318 --> 00:02:18.653
NEVER FORGET THOSE WE LOST ON

00:02:18.654 --> 00:02:21.089
9/11, HEROES LIKE PETE'S FATHER.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:24.826
I WILL SAY PETE, NEVER FORGET.

00:02:24.827 --> 00:02:27.629
&gt;&gt; NEVER FORGET.

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:29.831
&gt;&gt; Greg: THAT IS LEGITIMATELY

00:02:29.832 --> 00:02:30.164
AWESOME.

00:02:30.165 --> 00:02:31.466
THERE WERE THREE WINNERS,

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:33.768
CRENSHAW FOR HIS RESPONSE TO A

00:02:33.769 --> 00:02:35.103
CARELESS COMMENT, "SNL" FOR

00:02:35.104 --> 00:02:37.205
FINDING A CLEVER WAY TO CLEAN UP

00:02:37.206 --> 00:02:39.107
A MESS AND AMERICA WERE BEING

00:02:39.108 --> 00:02:41.309
HANDED AN HONEST TO GOD'S

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:42.577
BLUEPRINT FOR DEALING WITH

00:02:42.578 --> 00:02:43.311
FUTURE OUTRAGES.

00:02:43.312 --> 00:02:44.912
INSTEAD OF RAMPING UP THE RAGE,

00:02:44.913 --> 00:02:45.847
IT DIALED BACK.

00:02:45.848 --> 00:02:49.050
WE'VE SET UP BEFORE IT'S BEYOND

00:02:49.051 --> 00:02:51.486
TIME TO STOP CHASING SCALPS,

00:02:51.487 --> 00:02:52.887
DEMANDING APOLOGIES AND THEN

00:02:52.888 --> 00:02:53.321
REFUSING THEM.

00:02:53.322 --> 00:02:57.425
HAVEN'T WE HAD ENOUGH OF THE MO

00:02:57.426 --> 00:02:57.725
MOB?

00:02:57.726 --> 00:02:59.027
I KNOW I HAVE.

00:02:59.028 --> 00:03:01.696
TO HEAR CRENSHAW INITIATED A NEW

00:03:01.697 --> 00:03:03.498
WAY FORWARD, EXPRESS YOUR

00:03:03.499 --> 00:03:06.167
OPINION, DON'T CONDEMN, AND SEE

00:03:06.168 --> 00:03:06.701
WHAT HAPPENS.

00:03:06.702 --> 00:03:08.436
"SNL" RESPONDED WITH HUMBLE,

00:03:08.437 --> 00:03:09.103
GOOD HUMOR.

00:03:09.104 --> 00:03:11.306
IT'S ALL GOOD AND DARE I SAY

00:03:11.307 --> 00:03:12.674
HUMAN.

00:03:12.675 --> 00:03:14.676
FINALLY A SKIT WORTH REPEATING.

00:03:14.677 --> 00:03:16.210
I THOUGHT, DANA, PERFECTLY

00:03:16.211 --> 00:03:17.712
EXECUTED ON BOTH SIDES.

00:03:17.713 --> 00:03:19.514
&gt;&gt; Dana: AND THEY KEPT IT A

00:03:19.515 --> 00:03:20.815
SECRET SO EVERYONE WAS

00:03:20.816 --> 00:03:21.182
SURPRISED.

00:03:21.183 --> 00:03:23.451
THAT HELPED.

00:03:23.452 --> 00:03:24.686
I FIND DAN CRENSHAW QUITE

00:03:24.687 --> 00:03:25.086
REFRESHING.

00:03:25.087 --> 00:03:27.655
I REMEMBER WHEN HE WAS IN A NINE

00:03:27.656 --> 00:03:28.690
PERSON PRIMARY.

00:03:28.691 --> 00:03:29.691
THERE WAS AN OPEN SEAT IN

00:03:29.692 --> 00:03:30.958
HOUSTON AND HE WAS TRYING TO GET

00:03:30.959 --> 00:03:32.093
ATTENTION.

00:03:32.094 --> 00:03:33.728
THERE WAS A WOMAN RUNNING ON THE

00:03:33.729 --> 00:03:34.495
REPUBLICAN SIDE.

00:03:34.496 --> 00:03:35.363
SHE WAS VERY, VERY WEALTHY AND

00:03:35.364 --> 00:03:37.065
SPENDING ALL SORTS OF MONEY.

00:03:37.066 --> 00:03:38.966
HE DIDN'T HAVE ANY MONEY TO RUN,

00:03:38.967 --> 00:03:41.502
SO AND WHAT HE DECIDED TO DO WAS

00:03:41.503 --> 00:03:43.905
RUN HIS DISTRICT, 25 MILES OVER

00:03:43.906 --> 00:03:46.040
FOUR DAYS AND TRY TO GET

00:03:46.041 --> 00:03:46.841
ATTENTION.

00:03:46.842 --> 00:03:48.309
I THINK WHAT'S HAPPENED IS

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:49.077
HOUSTON HAS FOUND ITSELF A GREAT

00:03:49.078 --> 00:03:51.379
NEW LEADER.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.848
THEY HAVE THIS CONGRESSMAN.

00:03:53.849 --> 00:03:55.183
POP CULTURE, IT'S NOT GOING TO

00:03:55.184 --> 00:03:58.486
BE NICE TO HIM FOREVER.

00:03:58.487 --> 00:03:59.854
TAKE THIS MOMENT.

00:03:59.855 --> 00:04:01.789
IT WAS A REALLY GOOD LESSON

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.858
ABOUT LEADERSHIP.

00:04:03.859 --> 00:04:04.726
I ALSO APPRECIATED THE

00:04:04.727 --> 00:04:06.861
SUGGESTION FOR WHAT TO SAY TO A

00:04:06.862 --> 00:04:07.195
SOLDIER.

00:04:07.196 --> 00:04:08.563
RATHER THAN THANK YOU FOR YOUR

00:04:08.564 --> 00:04:12.900
SERVICE, TO SAY NEVER FORGET.

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:13.368
I LIKE THIS.

00:04:13.369 --> 00:04:15.069
&gt;&gt; Greg: I THINK THIS NEEDS TO

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:16.804
BE REPOSTED EVERY TIME THERE'S A

00:04:16.805 --> 00:04:17.271
NEW OUTRAGE.

00:04:17.272 --> 00:04:19.107
THIS IS KIND OF HOW YOU SOLVE

00:04:19.108 --> 00:04:19.540
THE PROBLEM.

00:04:19.541 --> 00:04:21.876
&gt;&gt; Juan: YEAH, TO ME, IT WAS

00:04:21.877 --> 00:04:25.747
SO CLASSIC AND SO GOOD.

00:04:25.748 --> 00:04:27.949
I CAN'T GET OVER CRENSHAW.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:30.084
&gt;&gt; Nicole: YOU ARE AGREEING

00:04:30.085 --> 00:04:30.485
WITH GREG.

00:04:30.486 --> 00:04:31.753
&gt;&gt; Juan: IT'S NOT OFTEN BUT IT

00:04:31.754 --> 00:04:33.654
DOES HAPPEN.

00:04:33.655 --> 00:04:35.857
I THOUGHT DAN CRENSHAW WAS SUPER

00:04:35.858 --> 00:04:36.190
CLASSY.

00:04:36.191 --> 00:04:38.059
I THOUGHT HE WAS CLASSY FROM THE

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:38.359
START.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:39.961
I THOUGHT WHEN HE SAID I DON'T

00:04:39.962 --> 00:04:40.828
NEED AN APOLOGY.

00:04:40.829 --> 00:04:41.963
PEOPLE SAY SILLY STUFF ALL THE

00:04:41.964 --> 00:04:42.263
TIME.

00:04:42.264 --> 00:04:45.433
I THINK IT WAS REALLY, YOU KNOW,

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:47.168
ABOVE AND BEYOND FOR HIM TO

00:04:47.169 --> 00:04:48.403
ACTUALLY COME TO NEW YORK AND GO

00:04:48.404 --> 00:04:49.137
ON THE SHOW AND GO THROUGH THE

00:04:49.138 --> 00:04:51.239
WHOLE THING.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:53.841
I JUST THOUGHT IT WAS TERRIFIC.

00:04:53.842 --> 00:04:55.710
WHAT'S INTERESTING TO ME ABOUT

00:04:55.711 --> 00:04:56.911
CRENSHAW IS HE'S NOT YOUR

00:04:56.912 --> 00:04:58.246
PROTOTYPICAL POLITICIAN.

00:04:58.247 --> 00:05:00.281
HE'S A GUY WHO WAS A REPUBLICAN

00:05:00.282 --> 00:05:02.283
BUT HE'S BEEN HIGHLY CRITICAL OF

00:05:02.284 --> 00:05:02.984
PRESIDENT TRUMP, FOR EXAMPLE.

00:05:02.985 --> 00:05:04.919
IT STRIKES ME THAT WE NEED MORE

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.954
PEOPLE LIKE THIS IN PUBLIC

00:05:06.955 --> 00:05:08.256
OFFICE.

00:05:08.257 --> 00:05:10.057
&gt;&gt; Greg: A VETERAN ESPECIALLY.

00:05:10.058 --> 00:05:11.092
&gt;&gt; Juan: ESPECIALLY ON

00:05:11.093 --> 00:05:11.526
VETERANS DAY.

00:05:11.527 --> 00:05:13.661
I THINK THERE'S A CLASS OF 12 OR

00:05:13.662 --> 00:05:14.362
SOMETHING VETERANS COMING IN

00:05:14.363 --> 00:05:16.831
THIS TIME.

00:05:16.832 --> 00:05:17.965
SEEING MORE VETERANS AND MORE

00:05:17.966 --> 00:05:19.066
FEMALE VETERANS AND I THINK

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:20.134
THAT'S A GOOD THING.

00:05:20.135 --> 00:05:25.206
IN FACT, THERE'S A PAC THAT

00:05:25.207 --> 00:05:28.075
PROMOTES VETERANS RUNNING.

00:05:28.076 --> 00:05:28.743
VETERANS KNOW EACH OTHER IN

00:05:28.744 --> 00:05:31.679
MOMENTS OF REAL THREAT AS

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:32.046
AMERICANS.

00:05:32.047 --> 00:05:33.214
&gt;&gt; Greg: IN REALITY.

00:05:33.215 --> 00:05:34.348
&gt;&gt; Dana: THEY DON'T CARE IF

00:05:34.349 --> 00:05:35.883
THEY ARE REPUBLICAN OR DEMOCRAT.

00:05:35.884 --> 00:05:38.252
&gt;&gt; Lawrence: IT WAS A GREAT

00:05:38.253 --> 00:05:38.686
MOMENT.

00:05:38.687 --> 00:05:39.720
SOMETHING THAT COUNTRY CAN

00:05:39.721 --> 00:05:40.054
EMBRACE.

00:05:40.055 --> 00:05:44.459
I DON'T THINK IT WAS NECESSARY,

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:44.859
PERSONALLY.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:46.694
I THINK SO OFTEN PEOPLE ON THE

00:05:46.695 --> 00:05:47.395
WRITER ON ON THE RECEIVING END

00:05:47.396 --> 00:05:53.067
OF THIS AND THE TONE NORMALLY IS

00:05:53.068 --> 00:05:54.469
TO FIRE THAT PERSON, GET RID OF

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:55.870
IT OR GO THAT PERSON.

00:05:55.871 --> 00:05:57.438
YOU SAY ONE THING AND IT

00:05:57.439 --> 00:05:58.005
DESTROYS YOUR CAREER.

00:05:58.006 --> 00:06:01.476
I DON'T WANT TO GET ON CONSTANT

00:06:01.477 --> 00:06:01.909
APOLOGY TOURS.

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:05.213
I'VE SEEN IT ON COLLEGE CAMPUSE

00:06:05.214 --> 00:06:05.580
CAMPUSES.

00:06:05.581 --> 00:06:06.881
THE MOB IT WILL TAKE OVER

00:06:06.882 --> 00:06:08.549
SOMETHING SO SIMPLE THAT

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:09.717
COULD'VE BEEN HANDLED BEHIND

00:06:09.718 --> 00:06:10.251
CLOSED DOORS.

00:06:10.252 --> 00:06:12.620
GOOD GESTURE, VERY POLITE, COOL

00:06:12.621 --> 00:06:14.322
TO SEE.

00:06:14.323 --> 00:06:17.658
I'M JUST NOT BIG ON THE

00:06:17.659 --> 00:06:18.659
CELEBRATION OF IT.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:20.361
&gt;&gt; Greg: YOU THINK IT'S MORE

00:06:20.362 --> 00:06:22.263
OF AN ISOLATED INCIDENT.

00:06:22.264 --> 00:06:23.664
&gt;&gt; Lawrence: QUITE FRANKLY IT

00:06:23.665 --> 00:06:24.899
WAS FOREST.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:25.333
IT WAS FORCED.

00:06:25.334 --> 00:06:27.268
THE EXECUTIVES CALLED HIM IN AND

00:06:27.269 --> 00:06:28.369
SAID YOU HAVE TICKED OFF THE

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:28.736
VETERANS.

00:06:28.737 --> 00:06:30.271
YOU'VE GOT TO DO SOMETHING TO

00:06:30.272 --> 00:06:31.472
MAKE IT RIGHT.

00:06:31.473 --> 00:06:34.108
IF IT WASN'T ABOUT THAT, THEY

00:06:34.109 --> 00:06:35.243
WOULD'VE DONE IT BEHIND CLOSED

00:06:35.244 --> 00:06:37.078
DOORS.

00:06:37.079 --> 00:06:38.679
&gt;&gt; Dana: IT WAS ON THE

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:39.113
TELEPROMPTER.

00:06:39.114 --> 00:06:41.015
IT'S NOT LIKE IT WAS A SLIP OF

00:06:41.016 --> 00:06:41.449
THE TONGUE.

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:43.484
&gt;&gt; Nicole: I LOVE THE WAY WHEN

00:06:43.485 --> 00:06:44.185
I'M SEEING FROM CONGRESSMAN

00:06:44.186 --> 00:06:46.087
ELECT DAN CRENSHAW.

00:06:46.088 --> 00:06:47.588
I THINK IT'S GREAT THAT HE WENT

00:06:47.589 --> 00:06:49.090
ON "SNL" AND HAD A LITTLE OLD

00:06:49.091 --> 00:06:49.690
FUN WITH IT.

00:06:49.691 --> 00:06:52.660
SHOWS HIS PERSONALITY.

00:06:52.661 --> 00:06:54.829
SHOWS WHAT HE'S GOING TO DO.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.497
I THINK PETE'S DAVIDSON APOLOGY

00:06:56.498 --> 00:06:57.298
WAS MEDIOCRE AT BEST.

00:06:57.299 --> 00:06:58.366
I WISH WE DIDN'T GET TO THE

00:06:58.367 --> 00:06:59.667
POINT WHERE THERE WAS AN

00:06:59.668 --> 00:07:00.001
APOLOGY.

00:07:00.002 --> 00:07:02.303
I DON'T KNOW IF WE NEEDED ONE.

00:07:02.304 --> 00:07:04.572
I CAN'T BELIEVE THE COMMENT CAME

00:07:04.573 --> 00:07:05.907
OUT OF HIS MOUTH.

00:07:05.908 --> 00:07:06.641
HIS FATHER DIED ON 9/11 WHEN HE

00:07:06.642 --> 00:07:11.846
WAS A YOUNG BOY AND DAN CRENSHAW

00:07:11.847 --> 00:07:14.181
LOST HIS EYE HIS THIRD COMBAT

00:07:14.182 --> 00:07:14.482
TOUR.

00:07:14.483 --> 00:07:17.285
HE'S GOING TO MOCK HIM FOR THAT?

00:07:17.286 --> 00:07:19.287
I DON'T UNDERSTAND WHERE THE

00:07:19.288 --> 00:07:19.787
THOUGHT PROCESSES.

00:07:19.788 --> 00:07:20.488
IT WAS NOT OFF THE CUFF.

00:07:20.489 --> 00:07:22.957
IT WAS A WRITTEN STATEMENT.

00:07:22.958 --> 00:07:25.426
I CAN'T WRAP MY HEAD OR ON THE

00:07:25.427 --> 00:07:27.328
FACT THAT THEY THOUGHT IT WAS

00:07:27.329 --> 00:07:27.628
OKAY.

00:07:27.629 --> 00:07:28.729
&gt;&gt; Greg: I WILL GO BACK TO MY

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:29.664
DEFENSE, EVEN THOUGH I SAID IT

00:07:29.665 --> 00:07:32.700
WAS A LOUSY JOKE.

00:07:32.701 --> 00:07:34.468
FOR SOME TYPES OF HUMOR, THE

00:07:34.469 --> 00:07:36.704
HUMOR IS IN THE FACT THAT IT'S

00:07:36.705 --> 00:07:38.272
AWFUL, THAT YOU'RE SAYING

00:07:38.273 --> 00:07:39.507
SOMETHING SO OBJECTIONABLE IT

00:07:39.508 --> 00:07:40.408
CAN'T BE REAL.

00:07:40.409 --> 00:07:42.910
&gt;&gt; Nicole: IF IT CAME FROM

00:07:42.911 --> 00:07:43.911
ANYPLACE OTHER THAN "SNL" WHO

00:07:43.912 --> 00:07:45.479
MAKES A MOCKERY OF REPUBLICANS

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:48.149
EVERY WEEK, MAYBE I WOULD SEE A

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:48.950
LITTLE BIT OF HUMOR IN IT AS

00:07:48.951 --> 00:07:54.256
LONG AS DAN CRENSHAW DID AS WELL

